# ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
# ║  Local stacks — copy to docker-compose.override.yml          ║
# ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝
#
# Docker Compose automatically reads `docker-compose.override.yml` next to the
# main file and merges it in. The real file is gitignored: it exists to run
# services on ONE machine that do not belong to this repository — a separate
# project, or something you are only trying out.
#
# WHY NOT A BRANCH
#
# Keeping a local service on a dedicated branch looks convenient and has an
# unpleasant side effect: switch back to another branch and the service keeps
# running, but no file declares it any more. Docker then treats it as an
# "orphan" container of the project, and `make up` — which passes
# `--remove-orphans` — deletes it without asking.
#
# This has already happened on this infrastructure: a container stayed up for
# weeks with its mounted directories by then empty and the compose file that
# defined it gone from disk, so it could no longer be recreated.
#
# A gitignored override does not have that problem: the service stays declared
# on this machine whichever branch is checked out.
#
# NOTES
#
# - Paths inside an included file resolve relative to THAT file's directory,
#   not to the repository root: a `build: context: .` in
#   /path/my-service/compose.yml builds from /path/my-service.
# - Put it somewhere the user running the stack can write: /opt belongs to root
#   on a standard Ubuntu install.
# - The `homelab` network is defined in docker-compose.yml and inherited
#   through the merge; included files must not redeclare it, or the include
#   conflicts.
# - Variables the local service needs go in this machine's .env.
#   `make check-env` will report them as extra compared to .env.example: that
#   is expected and correct — they are not repository configuration.

# A project living in its own repository, outside this tree:
include:
  - /path/to/separate-project/compose.yml

# Or a service declared directly here:
# services:
#   something-im-trying:
#     image: some/image:1.2.3
#     restart: unless-stopped
#     networks:
#       - homelab
